WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  the legendary rock band The Eagles is  suing a hotel in Mexico for using the  same name as its iconic song Hotel  California the band filed a trademark  infringement lawsuit against the Hotel  California in Baja the lawsuit says the  band has no connection to the hotel and  it also claims that the tourist  destination is using the Eagles classic  hit to mislead customers Carter Evans is  outside the hotel that is actually  associated with the famous tune that is  the Beverly Hills Hotel in Beverly Hills  California Carter good morning good  morning that's right this is actually  the hotel on the cover of that mega hit  1976 album Hotel California but when the  Mexican state of Baja had its own Hotel  California while the eagle swooped right  in with a lawsuit  there's plenty of room at the Hotel  California  but not apparently if you're misleading  consumers are selling unauthorized  branded merchandise that's the gist of  an 11-page lawsuit filed this week by  the Eagles against Hotel California AHA  in Mexico  according to the suit defendants lead US  consumers to believe that the hotel is  associated with the Eagles and among  other things served as the inspiration  for the lyrics in Hotel California which  is false Gayle King spoke with Eagle Don  Henley last year about where the song's  inspiration came from and it's not  really about California it's about  America you know it's about the dark  underbelly of the American Dream it's  about excess the group says the Baja  hotel is now making excessive use of the  words Hotel California  Melissa Doug addo is a trademark and  copyright attorney they're alleging a  couple things the first thing is that  the hotel is actually advertised in a  manner to create confusion in the minds  of consumers about the hotel being  affiliated with the band the Eagles the  [Music]  hotel's website references specific  lyrics in the song Hotel California is  accessed by driving down a long desert  highway and mission bells are heard  daily online reviews seem to corroborate  the band's claim the famous song by the  Eagles lured us here and the song made  this into a popular place and it's  interesting to tour those online reviews  that show actual confusion are very  significant and when you have real  evidence from real consumers that is  really terrific evidence also included  in the Eagles complaint the baja hotels  sale of merchandise like shirts caps and  keychains with the words hotel  california a phrase the band claims it  owns the legal rights to more than a  year ago the hotel filed for trademarks  for nearly 200 more Hotel California  products everything from fragrances to I  wear in bedspreads so I think that's the  reason for the swift action and the very  serious action that they've taken in  this lawsuit  well the BAA hotel told us it would have  no official comment until it answers  this  complaint but on its website it states  the owners do not have any affiliation  with the Eagles nor do they have any  association or promote any association  gail whatever the outcome it's a really  good song Thank You Carter

